============================================================
5. DAILY HUMAN COMMIT MESSAGE
============================================================

Normally, make ONE commit per repository per working day.

Before creating the commit, review the changes since the previous commit and,
when available, the day's Issue files to understand the overall work completed.

The commit message should be a GENERIC, HUMAN-WRITTEN summary of the day's
overall implementation for that repository, not a narrow description of only
one individual change.

The commit message may be different for each repository depending on the work
actually completed in that repository.

Good examples:
fix: improve bartender workflow and responsive web experience
feat: update daily check-in and session management improvements
fix: refine frontend UI and operational workflow
feat: improve backend session and synchronization handling

Bad:
update
changes
fixed
latest
test

