8. COMMAND DISPLAY FORMAT
============================================================

After reading this file, checking actual changes, and determining the affected
repositories, provide Git commands as SEPARATE COPY-PASTE CODE BLOCKS.

Do NOT combine all repositories into one large command block.

All commands must start and finish at the MONOREPO ROOT:
- Central repository commands run directly from the monorepo root.
- Dedicated repositories (web-frontend, backend, frontend) use normal push by
  entering the folder with `cd <folder>`, running status, add, commit, push,
  and immediately returning with `cd ..`.
- NEVER use `git subtree` or `subtree split` (which outputs slow numeric tick bars like `44/456 (43) [0]`).
  Always use clean, standard `cd <folder>` -> `cd ..` workflow.

Only display command blocks for repositories that actually have relevant changes.

Each affected repository must have its own complete command block containing:

For CENTRAL:
git status
git add <files>
git commit -m "<message>"
git push personal-repo main

For DEDICATED (web-frontend, backend, frontend):
cd <folder>
git status
git add .
git commit -m "<message>"
git push origin main
cd ..

