12. SENSITIVE & ENVIRONMENT FILES POLICY (.ENV & .ENV.EXAMPLE)
============================================================

NEVER push:
- .env
- .env.*
- .env*.local
- .env.example
- *.env
- *.env.example

to ANY of the 4 Git repositories (Central, Backend, Web Frontend, or React Native).

Always ensure:
1. Every repository root and subproject has `.gitignore` explicitly listing:
   .env
   .env.*
   .env*.local
   .env.example
   *.env
   *.env.example

2. Before staging or committing, verify that no `.env` or `.env.example` files are tracked:
   git status
   git ls-files | grep -i "\.env"

3. If any `.env` or `.env.example` file is ever accidentally staged, immediately unstage and remove it:
   git rm --cached <file>

